    <!-- FROM PROMPT TO WORKFLOW -->
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="path-title">
      <div class="band__inner">
        <h2 id="path-title" class="display display--sm">From prompt to workflow</h2>
        <div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>Each step came from a problem the previous step could not solve. That path shapes how I advise on AI: start small, learn what the work actually needs, then build the next layer.</p>
          </div>
          <dl class="ledger" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">1. Prompt engineering</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">On client engagements, I wrote prompts by hand for messaging, content, and SEO analysis. The repeated effort showed me that the work needed a dedicated agent.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">2. A purpose-built agent</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">I built an agent trained on copywriting practice, then added messaging, research, and brand guidelines. Using it showed me that one agent could not carry strategy, quality control, and production at once.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">3. An agentic workflow</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">I split the work across specialized agents with defined handoffs and independent quality gates, so each stage owns one kind of failure.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

