    <!-- HOW I APPROACH AI STRATEGY -->
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
      <div class="band__inner">
        <h2 id="approach-title" class="display display--sm">How I approach AI strategy</h2>
        <div>
          <dl class="ledger">
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">Start with the process</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">Map the work as it happens today, and find where a delay, a handoff, or a repeated judgment costs the most.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">Decide where an agent belongs</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">Not every step needs one. Agents earn their place where the work is repeatable and the quality bar can be written down.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">Govern the output</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">Give each failure mode its own gate, whether that is audience fit, accuracy, brand voice, or how readers and AI systems will receive the result.</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="ledger__row">
              <dt class="ledger__term">Plan for adoption from day one</dt>
              <dd class="ledger__def">A tool nobody uses returns nothing. Training, access, and a clear first use case matter as much as the build.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

